cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Finality-aware planning: deciding under uncertain payment finality"
abstract: "A planning policy over the FinalityBench environment that replaces a fixed escalate-to-a-human rule with an expected-value comparison over the dispositions available when a payment capture will not resolve before the order's ship-by deadline. Includes a belief over resolution time fitted from the benchmark's public split, a safety shield with expected-value and downside criteria, and the finding that an expected-value shield cannot refuse a gamble that is profitable in expectation."
